counterfactuals.output:
1. A tire demounting apparatus for removing a tire from a wheel rim, comprising:

a support configured to be positioned adjacent to the wheel rim;

a pair of mutually parallel plates carried by the support and spaced apart from one another;

an elongate hook arranged at least partially between the pair of mutually parallel plates and configured to engage a bead of the tire;

a transverse pin connected to the elongate hook and extending transversely with respect to the elongate hook; and

shaped guide tracks formed in the pair of mutually parallel plates, the transverse pin being received in and movable along the shaped guide tracks,

wherein movement of the transverse pin along the shaped guide tracks guides the elongate hook for roto-translational movement relative to the support between a tire-engaging position and a tire-demounting position.
